# Strategy technology tests.
# Format:
# scenario NAME
# terrain hills=N rocks=N grass=N water=N
# resources animals=N stone=N crops=N
# context visible=N flat=N fresh=N forest=N desert_snow=N resources=N minerals=N city=N settler=N
# birdsview x=N y=N civ=N military=N height=N resource=N
#   x/y are cells in the 50x50 strategic map. height is the compact landscape signal:
#   negative sea/water, near zero flat land, positive hills/rocks/forests.
#   resource is the primary resource id in that birdsview cell, using the game_prehistory.js resource table.
# tech opened=N
# expect technology Mining|Animal_Husbandry|Masonry|Irrigation
# end

scenario hills_choose_mining
terrain hills=0.70 rocks=0.10 grass=0.30 water=0.05
resources animals=0.05 stone=0.05 crops=0.10
birdsview x=20 y=20 civ=0 military=0 height=0.62 resource=0
tech opened=0.00
expect technology Mining
end

scenario rocks_choose_mining
terrain hills=0.25 rocks=0.60 grass=0.25 water=0.05
